        "access": "public",
        "description": "<p>The Cycle Facility Network Map&nbsp;<a target='_blank' href='https://data-atgis.opendata.arcgis.com/search?tags=Cycling' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'>data</a>&nbsp;viewable and downloadable here, shows the location of cycle facilities of all types across Auckland. This is a comprehensive view of the current built network and consists of cycle facilities provided by Auckland Transport, NZTA and Auckland Council.</p><div>&nbsp;</div><div>This data feeds into the publicly available on the&nbsp;<a target='_blank' href='https://mahere.at.govt.nz/portal/apps/experiencebuilder/experience/?id=0547bd817663487f9c148da9da284933' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'>Auckland Cycleway Map</a>. This map shows cycle routes across the city and is provided to help you plan your rides. The map highlights the different types of infrastructure on each of the routes and shows on-road cycles lanes, on-road protected cycle lanes, shared paths and quiet routes.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Cycleways form part of our future strategic network called&nbsp;<a target='_blank' href='https://at.govt.nz/media/1987213/fc_cycle-and-micromobility-v1.pdf' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'>The Cycle and Micromobility Strategic Network</a>, which is made up of the most important corridors that link to key destinations.&nbsp;</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div><p>More details about the future strategic cycling and micromobility network and how it links to other modes is available at&nbsp;<a target='_blank' href='https://at.govt.nz/about-us/transport-plans-strategies/future-connect-auckland-transports-network-plan' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'>Future Connect- Auckland Transport's Network Plan</a>.<br />&nbsp;</p><div>&nbsp;</div></div>",
